  "body": "https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#origin says, in some cases, to:\n\n> return a new globally unique identifier\n\nWhat does this mean? Is it a string with randomly-generated hexadecimal digits like `{21EC2020-3AEA-4069-A2DD-08002B30309D}`? https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Globally_unique_identifier Either way the spec should define this, or refer to something that does.\n",
